974 they've  been tinkering with where they kicked  the ball off probably used to be the 40  yard line and then his kickers got  better and better they moved it back to  get more returns you know because back  then nobody really you know knew  anything about player safety it was it  was a different world back then so  they've they've it's evolved much over  the last 20 years at least  but what about  the violence on touchbacks because I  tell people you're just watching the  football you're not watching the  collisions upfront where this might be  the only play you're in in the game or  you might be on the field for four plays  and their kickoffs you want to get your  money's worth if you're out there  playing don't you that's right I mean  yeah you know you're not gonna go half  speed just because you don't think  they'll run it out of the end zone and  you know that's the way it's like I said  I mean these guys are out there to  compete at the highest level they don't  care if it's for money or marbles or  chalk they're gonna win every play they  can and that's you know there's no  escaping and that's why I think it's you  know the evolution is going to continue  downward till it's it's drastically  different than it has been how unsafe is  the punt return  well the punt return is kind of the same  same situation although it's a little  safer punt return team is one of those  it's the same thing yet guys run in a  lot of open space they get caught off  guard because they're either looking up  and trying to find the ball or looking  around trying to find the returner and  they get lit up and that's the kind of  thing that is second only to kickoff  return as this part return is being you  know the most unsafe and where you get a  lot of injuries and while the  differences you know statistically is  kind of miniscule it there is a  significant difference between those and  regular down a distance place so I don't  know that they'll do too much with punt  punt return because there is a  significant difference in that's those  stats and injuries but they they're  looking at everything now and trying to  give or come up with creative and more  fun alternatives would you have had a  career if there weren't kick homes  probably not probably not but then again  damn they don't owe me a job I mean I  evolved  I had great coaches who found a role for  me and I tried to make myself valuable  but it's not like they're cutting the  teams if you don't who kicked off you're  gonna cut five guys off the roster  there's still gonna be five jobs there  for guys who wouldn't have had a job had  to kick off stayed around so you get  that sort of cuts both ways now they  start talking about making the rosters  35 instead of 45  then I'd have a problem with it but  they're not taking jobs away they're  just changing roles I don't have a real  problem with that I when I work with  Rodney Harrison and of course he was a  violent player he would he watches now  and he says I don't know how I played  that game and I'm curious you're down on  the sidelines for all of these games and  I tell these guys they get the guys I  work they get tired of hearing this if  you heard the game on the sidelines you  didn't have to watch it just hear it  you'd never let your kid play football  it's so it's so vile it's so different  down there Steve yeah you're right I  mean I tell people if you've ever if you  ever get a chance to watch the game on  the sidelines don't do it you'll never  watch first you'll never want to watch  it anyplace else and secondly you see  the size and the speed of these guys  it'll turn their insides to water I mean  it it is a different game but by the  same token I'm I'm a big proponent of  youth football I think it's a great idea  no question there is a physical risk but  I have four sons they all played and  they all got great benefit out of it and  I think that's one of the things that I  say to moms who ask me I say let your  kids play when they're little and make  them quit when they're 15 because once  they cross the bridge of adulthood and  turn and go past puberty then they start  to play angry but up until then there's  so many positive benefits from the use  for that particularly football that I  think because of the risk is there I  think the benefit is ten times more than  the risk there is to injury I I'm a big  proponent of the game specifically for  youth but when they get older and  heavier and faster and stronger that's  when it becomes the game you and I watch  on the sidelines and it's not for the  faint of heart  Steve thanks for joining us we  appreciate your time then I appreciate  it good talking to you Steve Tasker CBS  sports seven-time Pro Bowl special  teamer probably wouldn't had a career at  least at the Pro Bowl level without the  kickoff for more Dan Patrick show to the  audience Channel 239 on DirecTV or  download the Dan Patrick show app  you  [Music]
 

